    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d868">

                <pb facs="1006" n="994" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg994"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00114A Pacific War/503: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-16">June 16, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1479. American interests—Japan. Domei<anchor n="72" xml:id="d868-f1"/> has
                    reported that punishment has been meted out by Japanese to 25 members American
                    armed forces who have recently revealed their identity after being held as
                    civilians in the Philippines. Request Swiss authorities to endeavor to verify
                    this report, to obtain names of men, and to report the nature of the
                        punishment.<anchor n="73" xml:id="d868-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d868-f1" n="72" xml:id="d868-f1-content">
                <p>Japanese official news agency.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d868-f2" n="73" xml:id="d868-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 7544, December 1, the Minister in Switzerland reported that the
                    Swiss Legation in Tokyo verified the report that 25 soldiers interned at Santo
                    Tomas were condemned to 2 months’ imprisonment for offense as stated and
                    interned in POW camp in the Philippines after serving sentences
                    (711.11B114A/121).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
